                <pb facs="0303" n="197" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg197"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Egan to Mr.
                            Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-10-26"><hi rendition="#italic">October 26,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Egan states that he has communicated the Department’s telegram of the 23d
                    instant to the minister for foreign affairs, and asks what reparation will be
                    expected if the facts be as reported by Capt. Schley.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
